Hello,

On 10/31/2010 12:20 AM, Wolfgang Karall wrote:
> One thing I forgot to mention in the intial mail is that what I think the
> problem might be is that the disks spin up one after the other in this
> NAS box (both when powering on, but also at reboots there is a audible
> delay), and the old version 2.6.26 waited long enough while the newer
> versions don't. At least that's what I gather from the "retrying in
> 5 secs" lines.

Finally got around to testing this out further (on both version 2.6.32 
and 2.6.36), and this is indeed a timing issue. Adding a simple "sleep" 
to my initramfs setup (as init-top script) led to the drives all being 
recognized properly again, see the attached dmesg outputs.

Glad this can be worked around in userland at least.

Cheers
Wolfgang

